{{Top|legends=Snubfighter/Legends}}
{{Quote|A small one-man fighter should be able to penetrate the outer defense.''"<br />"''Pardon me for asking, sir, but what good are snub-fighters going to be against ''that''?|Jan Dodonna and Jon Vander, referring to the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] battle station|<ref name="A New Hope">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
[[File:Swarm_Tactics_XWM_2017_Q1_Tournament_Kit.png|thumb|right|250px|The Rebel Alliance made use of X-wing and B-wing snub-fighters.]]
'''Snub-fighter''' was a term used to describe small [[starfighter]]s<ref name="A New Hope" /> such as the [[Z-95 Headhunter]],<ref name="Clone Z-95 Starfighter">{{Databank|clone-z-95-starfighter|Clone Z-95 starfighter}}</ref> its successor, the [[T-65B X-wing starfighter]], the [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber]],<ref name="A New Hope" /> the [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter|B-wing]],<ref name="BS: Kuat">{{InsiderCite|168|Blade Squadron: Kuat}}</ref> the [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter]], and the [[TIE/sf space superiority fighter]].<ref name="TLJ">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

